  "head": "f4d39d7aa5fba4817493b617f66103f385df8190 (was bb41814b8)",
  "summary": "All three owed items landed, and the open executor key, the alias refusal and the block-by-reference stand exactly as reviewed. (a) A new D2 conversion, page-action-row-navigation-executor-to-url, sits in MAJOR_18_CONVERSIONS. It is inserted where its identifier sorts (between objectTenancyOrganizationFieldRemoved and pageAssignedProfilesRemoved), at order 63, and defined directly above pageAssignedProfilesRemoved. It has retiredFromLoadPath: true and retiredAfter: '17.7.0', which is both the label when it was written and, under the 18.0.0-next.0 label main now carries, the newest stable release; retired-after.census.test.ts is green. Through mapPageComponents it renames the value 'navigation' to 'url' on action:button / action:icon properties.actionType and on action:group / action:menu properties.actions[].type. It is copy-on-write (untouched members keep their identity), idempotent by construction, and has a disjoint fixture pair (5 notices: button, icon, group member, nested menu member, slotted header icon). Every other executor value, an element:button inline action, a non-object member and a non-array actions are left alone. Its own test file pins the stored-row seam on all four shapes, the parse after the rewrite, the controls, the same reference back, idempotence, and that the authoring funnel does not replay it. The D3 entry ui-page-action-row-navigation-executor-refused now carries conversionIds naming it, and its reason no longer skips the conversion on a census. The changeset's FROM → TO rows and its one-line fix name os migrate meta --write as the rewrite; the onSuccess leg stays by hand. Step 18's rationale gains one fragment, sorted by id, at order 95. (b) refuseUnopenableRowUrlTarget's docblock now guarantees only rows whose EXECUTOR KEY names the url navigator. It states that a row with no executor key dispatches on name, which is #23168's question. refuseRowUrlExecutorAlias's docblock names the conversion. (c) #23146 landed (02bec6ca86), so expression-scope-data-root.pin.test.ts gains one TSDoc-face assertion for the page:tabs twin: it says 'the component-node evaluator mounts no `data` root' and carries neither retired claim shape. Turso: the CI red does not reproduce. driver-turso's whole suite is green at bb41814b8, the failing head (88 files, 2373 passed, 33 skipped), and again at de990e9bf, 8ec1d54a5 and f4d39d7aa with the same counts. The failing case cannot be named from here: the job log's blob host is outside this container's proxy (GET .../actions/jobs/115135839279/logs was refused), and the check-run annotations carry only 'driver-turso pnpm run test exited (1)'. The diff reaches nothing in driver-turso, so per the order the seat counts this round's push as the one re-run. Merges: main came in twice through os-regen-merge.sh. The first, at e540e7ffb, conflicted only on the ledger header; I resolved it semantically to main's 234 schemas plus this branch's 4 sites, 759, and build-schemas agrees. The second, at d889448b9, was clean; it includes the Version Packages (next) landing, which moved the label to 18.0.0-next.0. main then moved 3 more commits (107853ced, c6139f264, 44e2d505c), none touching these 13 files, and the PR reads mergeable_state clean. A PR body change is owed. The exact text is in pr_body_edits, for the seat to write.",
  "items_from_to": [
    "② alias leg: FROM a D3 entry with 'No conversion is registered: the authored census finds no page action row writing navigation' and a changeset saying 'the rewrite is by hand'. TO the D2 conversion page-action-row-navigation-executor-to-url (retiredFromLoadPath, retiredAfter '17.7.0', order 63); the D3 entry with conversionIds: ['page-action-row-navigation-executor-to-url'] and a reason that names the conversion as the rewrite; and changeset rows and a one-line fix that name `os migrate meta --from 17 --write` as the rewrite for the executor, while the onSuccess leg stays by hand.",
    "① item 8: FROM 'so no row reaches the url navigator with its `target` unjudged'. TO 'so no row whose EXECUTOR KEY names the url navigator reaches it with its `target` unjudged. A row with no executor key at all is outside both rules: the runner then dispatches on the row's `name`, so `name: 'url'` reaches the same navigator with `target` judged only at the click — that leg is #23168's question, not settled here.'",
    "① item 5 (optional): FROM no TSDoc-face assertion. TO one test in expression-scope-data-root.pin.test.ts. It reads component.zod.ts between the 'Conditional tab (CEL, #2606)' anchor and the tab item's visibleWhen declaration, and asserts that the text contains 'the component-node evaluator mounts no `data` root' and carries neither RETIRED_CLAIM_SHAPES entry nor 'binds it to the data-source ADAPTER'."
  ],
  "turso_finding": "NOT REPRODUCED. driver-turso's full suite (pnpm exec vitest run --maxWorkers=2 in packages/drivers/driver-turso, after building its dependency closure) ran at bb41814b8, the failing CI head: 88 files, 2373 passed, 33 skipped, exit 0 (VERDICT command-exit 0, held 119s). It ran identically at de990e9bf, 8ec1d54a5 and f4d39d7aa. The failing case is not nameable from this container: the job log's storage host (productionresultssa0.blob.core.windows.net) is outside the proxy, and the check-run annotations for job 115135839279 say only 'command (packages/drivers/driver-turso) pnpm run test exited (1)'. No interaction with this diff was found: driver-turso imports @objectstack/spec/data, /contracts and /api only, and nothing in it names an action row, ComponentPropsMap or onSuccess. Reading: a flake in that shard, with the case unnamed. The seat's #17079 timing-window record is the likely signature, but that is not verified here.",
  "tests": "Final head f4d39d7aa. Every heavy run went through os-verify-lock and is read from its VERDICT line. The final verification batch (workspace build, five targeted spec files, spec full, lint full, the lint row pin, driver-turso): VERDICT command-exit 0, held 1368s. Inside it: workspace build 74/74; targeted spec 5 files / 313 passed (page-action-row-navigation-executor-to-url.test.ts, conversions.test.ts, retired-after.census.test.ts, component-action-row-on-success-executor.test.ts, expression-scope-data-root.pin.test.ts); spec full 663 files, 20149 passed, 1 todo; lint full 138 files, 6680 passed; the lint row pin 16/16; driver-turso 88 files, 2373 passed, 33 skipped. Typecheck: spec typecheck and lint typecheck, VERDICT command-exit 0. check:generated: 'All 14 generated artifacts are up to date', exit 0. Intermediate head de990e9bf: build plus 12 targeted files (including conversions-major18-merge.test.ts, step18-rationale-merge.test.ts and src/migrations) read 610 passed; spec full 663 / 20135; lint full 138 / 6636; driver-turso 2373 passed; all VERDICT command-exit 0. Ablations, src-only, through scripts/ablation-replace.mjs at de990e9bf. (C) node leg, guard compared to ablated-23103-conv-node: 3 failed / 261 passed (the fixture pair and both node stored-row pins). (D) member leg, container set emptied to ablated-23103-conv-member: 3 failed / 261 passed (the fixture pair and both member pins). Each was restored to blob 5795af427533 == HEAD with an empty git diff HEAD, and the tree was clean after. Round 1's A/B ablations stand. Gates: dispatch-gates --commands --repo objectstack-ai/objectstack derived 111 at f4d39d7aa; 110 ran, every exit recorded before any pipe, all exit 0 (the workspace was built first, so no prerequisite exit 3 this time). check:type-check-debt is NOT MEASURED, by order. --ran: '111 derived, 110 run, 1 NOT-MEASURED, 0 UNRUN'. check-adr-0087-registration registers both D3 ids. check:spec-changes reads 125 converted / 436 migrated (was 124). check:nul-bytes is green, and the raw control-byte scan of the 13 touched files finds 0 lines. Size: 13 files, +899/-37 = 936.",
  "mcp_calls": "0 — no MCP GitHub calls",
  "api_writes": "1 this round — this os-dev-report comment, through the fleet-write relay: POST /repos/objectstack-ai/objectstack/dispatches, executed as POST /repos/objectstack-ai/objectstack/issues/23103/comments. Plus git pushes of the branch (de990e9bf, 90dae0f12, 8ec1d54a5, f4d39d7aa; all fast-forward, not REST). No PR body write: the edits go to the seat as exact text.",
  "pr_body_edits": [
    {
      "find": "| `actionType` on `action:button` / `action:icon` | any string | any string except `'navigation'`, which is refused at `actionType` with the rename onto `'url'` |",
      "replace": "| `actionType` on `action:button` / `action:icon` | any string | any string except `'navigation'`, which is refused at `actionType` with the rename onto `'url'`; `os migrate meta --write` and the stored-row seam rewrite it (D2 `page-action-row-navigation-executor-to-url`) |"
    },
