      "replace": "The executor leg is lossless, so it also lands as the D2 conversion `page-action-row-navigation-executor-to-url`: `retiredFromLoadPath: true`, `retiredAfter: '17.7.0'`, in `MAJOR_18_CONVERSIONS` at order 63. The D3 entry names it in `conversionIds`. The `onSuccess` leg stays D3 only, because a refused address has no lossless rewrite."
    },
    {
      "find": "  - #23146 had not landed at the last push, so no TSDoc-face assertion was added to its `expression-scope-data-root.pin.test.ts`.",
      "replace": "  - #23146 landed (`02bec6ca86`), and `expression-scope-data-root.pin.test.ts` gains the TSDoc-face assertion for this `page:tabs` twin."
    },
    {
      "find": "  - The regenerated `component.mdx`, and two D3 entries.",
      "replace": "  - The regenerated `component.mdx`, and two D3 entries.\n  - From the fix round on contract review `6138862349`: the D2 entry in `conversions/registry.ts`, its test `page-action-row-navigation-executor-to-url.test.ts`, and its step-18 rationale fragment in `migrations/registry.ts.template`."
    },
    {
      "find": "This is the same family, reported in the dev report for the seat to place; it is not fixed here.",
      "replace": "This is the same family, carried by #23168, and it is not fixed here. `refuseUnopenableRowUrlTarget`'s docblock now scopes its guarantee to the executor key."
    },
    {
      "section": "## Verification record",
      "replace_whole_section_body_with": "All readings are at `f4d39d7aa` unless stated. That head is this branch merged with `origin/main` `d889448b9` through `scripts/pm/os-regen-merge.sh`; three later `main` commits touch none of these 13 files. Every heavy run went through `scripts/pm/os-verify-lock.sh`, and each result is its `VERDICT` line.\n\n- **Builds:**\n  - The workspace build: 74 / 74, exit 0.\n  - `@objectstack/spec check:generated`: \"All 14 generated artifacts are up to date\", exit 0.\n  - The ledger moved only by main's own sites: 234 / 759 after the merge, with this branch's four sites kept.\n- **Typecheck:** `@objectstack/spec typecheck` and `@objectstack/lint typecheck`, exit 0.\n- **Tests:**\n  - Spec, full: 663 files, 20149 passed, 1 todo.\n  - Lint, full: 138 files, 6680 passed.\n  - Five spec files, 313 passed: the conversion's own test, `conversions.test.ts`, `retired-after.census.test.ts`, the row pin and `expression-scope-data-root.pin.test.ts`.\n  - The lint row pin: 16 / 16.\n  - `driver-turso`: 88 files, 2373 passed, 33 skipped.\n- **Ablations:**\n  - Round 1's two, (A) the rows' `onSuccess` block and (B) the alias refusal, stand as recorded at `bb41814b8`.\n  - Round 2 adds two src-only ablations of the conversion, through `scripts/ablation-replace.mjs`, at `de990e9bf`. The node leg's guard was compared to `ablated-23103-conv-node`, and the member leg's container set was emptied.\n  - Each read 3 failed / 261 passed over the conversion test plus `conversions.test.ts`: the fixture pair, and that leg's two stored-row pins.\n  - Each was restored to blob == HEAD with an empty `git diff HEAD`.\n- **Gates:** `dispatch-gates --commands --repo objectstack-ai/objectstack` derived 111 at `f4d39d7aa`.\n  - 110 ran, all exit 0.\n  - `check:type-check-debt` is NOT MEASURED, by order.\n  - The `--ran` reconcile reads \"111 derived, 110 run, 1 NOT-MEASURED, 0 UNRUN\".\n  - `check-adr-0087-registration` registers both D3 ids. `check:spec-changes` reads 125 converted / 436 migrated.\n- **Size:** 13 files, +899 / -37 = 936 changed lines."
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [],
  "out_of_scope_findings": [
    "carrier: 承接者:无 · noted, not filed — CI job logs are unreadable from a cloud seat container: GET /repos/{o}/{r}/actions/jobs/{id}/logs redirects to productionresultssa0.blob.core.windows.net, outside the agent proxy, so a dev cannot name a failing CI case from here. That is an environment fact, not a repo defect."
  ],
  "deviations": [
    "Files beyond the claim's literal list, owed by the review's ②: packages/spec/src/conversions/registry.ts (the D2 entry), its test page-action-row-navigation-executor-to-url.test.ts, packages/spec/src/migrations/registry.ts.template (one STEP18_RATIONALE fragment, as the spec-property-retirement kit's step-18 item asks) and packages/spec/src/ui/expression-scope-data-root.pin.test.ts (item c).",
    "After the second merge (8ec1d54a5) I first rebuilt without reinstalling; main had moved pnpm-lock.yaml and packages/verify/package.json, so @objectstack/verify's DTS build failed (TS2307 @objectstack/metadata). I then ran pnpm install --frozen-lockfile, and the workspace built 74/74. The spec, lint and turso suites at 8ec1d54a5 had run before that reinstall; none of them depends on @objectstack/verify. The final head's numbers all come from runs after the reinstall.",
    "A local helper that ran gate commands through bash -c with a variable was refused by the harness's removal-safety check (it could not verify the script). I did not retry it; I ran the six gate commands one by one, literally, instead. No GitHub write was involved.",
    "main moved three commits after the final merge (107853ced, c6139f264, 44e2d505c). None touches these 13 files, so I did not merge again; the PR reads mergeable_state clean, and CI's merge ref covers the join."
  ]
